# LuwanTerm Licence

Version 1.0

Copyright (c) 2026 LuwanIO

## What this means, in short

This summary is here so you do not have to be a lawyer to know where you stand.
It is not the licence. The terms below are.

- **Use it for anything.** At home, at work, in a company, on a client's
  servers, in a data centre. Being paid for your job does not make your use of
  LuwanTerm a problem.
- **Read it, change it, share it.** Fork it, patch it, publish your fork, hand a
  copy to a colleague.
- **Contributions are welcome**, and you keep the copyright in what you write.
- **You may not sell it.** Not the software, not a paid product built around it,
  not a paid service that is really just this with a login, not paid support for
  it. If money is changing hands for LuwanTerm, that is not allowed.
- **You may not use it to hurt people.** Breaking into machines you have no
  right to, surveilling or harassing anyone, or trampling on human rights ends
  your licence immediately.

This is **source-available**, not open source as the Open Source Initiative
defines it, because a licence cannot restrict what you use software for and
still meet that definition. Everything is public and forkable. It is just not
for sale.

## Terms

### 1. Definitions

**"This software"** means LuwanTerm, in source or compiled form, together with
the documentation, configuration and assets distributed with it, and any part of
it.

**"You"** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
licence. **"Your"** has the matching meaning.

**"The licensor"** means the copyright holder named above and every contributor
who has licensed their contribution under these terms.

**"Sell"** means to supply, or offer to supply, this software or access to it,
or anything whose value depends substantially on it, in exchange for money or
other consideration. Being paid for your own time and work, on something that is
not this software, is not selling it.

**"Contribution"** means any work you deliberately submit to the licensor for
inclusion in this software.

### 2. Acceptance

To exercise any right under this licence, you must accept it. These terms are
conditions of the rights granted, and a limit on them. If you do not accept
these terms, you have no rights to this software.

### 3. Copyright licence

The licensor grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to use,
run, copy, display, modify and prepare derivative works of this software, for
any purpose, subject to sections 7 and 8.

Your purpose may be a commercial one. Using this software in the course of a
business, in paid employment, for a client, or to run infrastructure you are
paid to run, is expressly permitted. Section 7 restricts selling this software,
not working for a living with it.

### 4. Distribution licence

The licensor grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to
distribute this software, and works derived from it, subject to sections 7 and
8, and provided you comply with section 9.

### 5. Changes and new works

You may make changes and build new works based on this software. Your changes
and new works are covered by this licence to the extent they contain any of this
software, and you must license them under these same terms when you distribute
them. What you write that stands entirely apart from this software is yours to
