### 6. Patent licence

The licensor grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive patent licence
under patents the licensor can license, to make, use, sell, offer for sale,
import and otherwise exploit this software, subject to sections 7, 8 and 12.

### 7. No selling

**You may not sell this software.** In particular, you may not:

1. sell copies of it, or charge a fee, subscription or royalty for it or for
   access to it;
2. include it in a product, bundle, distribution or device that is offered for
   a fee, where this software is part of what is being paid for;
3. operate it, or its functionality, as part of a hosted or managed service that
   is offered for a fee;
4. charge for support, maintenance, hosting, installation, integration or
   customisation of this software;
5. put any part of it behind a payment, licence key, subscription or paywall; or
6. accept money or other consideration from anyone in exchange for any of the
   rights granted by this licence.

This does not stop you being paid for your own work. A consultant who sets up a
client's servers and uses LuwanTerm to do it is paid for the setup, not for
LuwanTerm, and is fine. A consultant who charges that client for LuwanTerm, or
for a support contract covering it, is not.

Voluntary donations to the licensor, and to contributors for their own work, are
not selling.

### 8. Acceptable use

This software must not be used to harm people. You may not use it, or anything
built from it:

1. to access, interfere with, disrupt or extract data from any computer,
   network, account or system without the clear authorisation of whoever is
   entitled to give it;
2. to surveil, track, profile or monitor any person without their informed
   consent, or to build or operate a system whose purpose is to do so;
3. to harass, stalk, threaten, intimidate, defame or incite violence against any
   person or group;
4. to deprive any person of, or infringe, their human or legal rights,
   including the rights set out in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights,
   the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights, the ILO Declaration
   on Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work, and the UN Convention on the
   Rights of the Child, as those instruments are applied to conduct within your
   control;
5. to discriminate against any person on the basis of a characteristic protected
   under the law that applies to you;
6. in connection with forced labour, human trafficking, or the exploitation of
   children; or
7. for any purpose that is unlawful where you are, or where the affected people
   are.

This software is a tool for administering systems you are responsible for.
Testing the security of a system you have written permission to test is
authorised use under paragraph 1; testing one you do not is not.

